should we think that these schools are "the worst."  After all, lots of
other schools have similarly outrageous anecdotes.

UPenn refused to take disciplinary action against black students who stole
newspapers (because of the content), but vigorously pursued the prosecution of
a student who shouted at some loud black students that they should go to the
zoo.

Several years ago Syracuse University allowed an official student group to
discriminate in violation of its regulations.  When called on it, the
administration actually changed the regulations to allow minority groups
to discriminate (until the Dept. of Education told them they were violating
the CRA of 1964).  They still turn a blind eye to it, because it's too
politically charged for them to take action.

I'm sure loads of other schools have similarly outrageous policies.  I can't
really find much meaning in declaring those listed above as "the worst."


