Having just gone through the application process last year with my oldest, I
can comment:

A student must apply separately to each individual campus of the University
of California. In addition to the overall criteria of the UC system, each 
campus has its own supplementary set of admission standards and criteria, which
they choose not to detail to the prospective students..i.e., a student may be
selected or rejected for  any  of the campuses without affecting his elegibil-
ty for the others. If the student does not accept within the allotted time, or
chooses to delay his matriculation, he must reapply.

